message.content:
Here’s the exact request you’d send to VirusTotal to fetch the *subdomains* relationship for `example.org`:

```
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects?relationship_type=subdomains&limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc
Headers:
  x-apikey: my_api
```

If the API returned two subdomains, the minimal payload you asked for (only IDs and any context attributes) would look like this:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "sub1.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "confidence": "high",
      "first_seen": "2024-01-15T12:34:56Z"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "sub2.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "confidence": "medium",
      "last_seen": "2024-02-20T08:22:13Z"
    }
  }
]
```

(If a particular subdomain has no context attributes, you can omit the `"context_attributes"` field or leave it empty.)

